# Redirects — Handbook §26.
#
# EVERY URL the predecessor site had that this one does not. The canonical-identity rule is not
# satisfied by choosing a domain: the old URLs are indexed, linked and bookmarked, and they are the
# traffic you already paid for.
#
# A host that cannot issue a real redirect status cannot do this at all. A markup page that
# refreshes the browser is not a redirect — it does not carry the same authority signal and does not
# work for anything that is not markup. That is why hosting is chosen BEFORE the first line of
# markup (§26).
#
# Syntax is the edge host's. 301 is permanent; use 302 only while genuinely temporary.
#
#   /old-path            /new-path              301
#   /old-section/*       /new-section/:splat    301
#   /retired-offer       /                      301

# Apex and www resolve to one canonical host. Which of the two is canonical is a decision, not a
# default — record it in brief.md.
